# SwiftUI View Composition

- Keep `body` small; extract subviews (as private `var` or nested `struct`) when a view grows.
- Put view logic in the view model; views should bind and layout, not decide business rules.
- Add `#Preview` where helpful for isolated iteration; prefer real dependencies or minimal fakes.
- Use `@ViewBuilder` only when needed (multiple conditional branches returning different view types).
- Prefer semantic modifiers and avoid unnecessary `Group` wrappers.
